Description: Auto DJ: transition length per transition and phrase alignment
 For a script that chooses the kind of each Auto DJ transition (DecksmithOS
 Auto DJ script): [AutoDJ],next_transition_beats >= 0 sets the length of the
 next transition in beats of the outgoing track (0 = a cut); it goes back to
 -1 (transition mode and time decide, as in stock Mixxx) when that
 transition starts. [AutoDJ],seconds_to_transition (read only) counts down
 to the start of the next transition (-1 = none planned, 0 = under way), so
 that a script can start effects before it. [AutoDJ],fade_now honours
 next_transition_beats too (a script that has stopped the outgoing track
 from reaching the planned start, with a loop roll or a brake, cuts with
 it).
 .
 [AutoDJ],phrase_align ([Auto DJ] PhraseAlign, default on): the transition
 starts on a phrase start of the outgoing track and the incoming track is
 cued at one of its phrase starts, so that both phrases begin together.
 Phrase starts come from the track structure (rekordbox or detected,
 patches 0007 / 0020); phrases longer than 8 bars are divided every 8 bars;
 tracks without phrases use every 8 bars from the first downbeat or beat.
 Tracks without a beat grid are left as the transition mode set them.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
